  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 402.06 Additional Information Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 402.06 Additional Information Required. If the dam will be a low hazard, significant hazard, or high hazard structure, the owner shall submit plans and specifications which shall, at a minimum, include the following:\n\n(a) Scaled plan view;\n\n(b) Scaled cross-sectional view of dam through the outlet, showing elevations of inlet and outlet, watertight connections, embankment material;\n\n(c) Design of and cover treatment for erosion-resistant embankment slopes;\n\n(d) Gradation analysis for all structural soils and fill materials to be used during construction;\n\n(e) Compaction specifications in accordance with Env-Wr 403.02(d) and (e);\n\n(f) Construction sequence;\n\n(g) Sufficient detail to show the location of the proposed work in relation to the entire dam; and\n\n(h) A written OMRF as described in Env-Wr 303.04.\n\nSource. #8414, eff 8-20-05; ss by #10510, eff 1-22-14; ss by #13980, eff 5-24-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html"
}
